=== quizzotic attempts --help ===
usage: quizzotic attempts <action> [flags]
actions:
  create           Answer a problem
  get              Get an attempt
  list             List attempts
  rate             Rate an attempt late

=== quizzotic attempts create --help ===
usage: quizzotic attempts create [flags]

Answer a problem

Records one attempt. In a single transaction the server grades the
response, stores the attempt and updates the card, then returns the
grade, the full answer, the explanation and the card's next due date
(`next_due`; null for an `open` attempt that has no rating yet).

`problem_version` must be the problem's current version (409
otherwise, so the client refetches); the problem must be `live`.

`response` depends on the problem type: `mcq` takes the selected
choice ids, `cloze` a map of blank id to typed text, `open` the typed
text. `rating` is optional for `mcq` and `cloze` (a right answer
defaults to Good, a wrong one is always Again) and required for
`open` to be scheduled. Rating 1 (Again) is invalid when the answer
is right: it returns 422 with an error on the `rating` field. An
attempt is never edited afterwards, except that a missing rating may
be filled in once.

Humans only: agent clients never hold `attempts:write` and get 403.

flags:
  --agent
      authenticate with the stored agent login (see quizzotic login --agent) (default false)
  --data
      request body: @file.json, or - for stdin
  --idempotency-key
      Client-chosen key; replays within 24 h return the original response. [sent as the Idempotency-Key header]
  --output
      output format: json or table (default json)
  --server
      server base URL (default $QUIZZOTIC_SERVER or http://localhost:8080)
  --set
      set a body field: key=value (repeatable; dotted keys nest; values parse as JSON when valid)

Authentication: QUIZZOTIC_TOKEN, a headless client (QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_ID + QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_SECRET),
or the stored login from "quizzotic login" (--agent for the agent login).

=== quizzotic attempts get --help ===
usage: quizzotic attempts get <id> [flags]

Get an attempt

Returns one of the caller's attempts. Agents with `attempts:read` may read.

arguments:
  <id>  Attempt ID.

flags:
  --agent
      authenticate with the stored agent login (see quizzotic login --agent) (default false)
  --output
      output format: json or table (default json)
  --server
      server base URL (default $QUIZZOTIC_SERVER or http://localhost:8080)

Authentication: QUIZZOTIC_TOKEN, a headless client (QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_ID + QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_SECRET),
or the stored login from "quizzotic login" (--agent for the agent login).

=== quizzotic attempts list --help ===
usage: quizzotic attempts list [flags]

List attempts

Lists the caller's attempts, oldest first (answer order), with cursor
pagination. Filters combine with AND. `problem` is a problem ID. `tag`
accepts a tag ID, slug or alias and keeps attempts at problems that
carry it. `since` (inclusive) and `until` (exclusive) are RFC 3339
timestamps bounding `answered_at`. Agents with `attempts:read` may
read.

flags:
  --agent
      authenticate with the stored agent login (see quizzotic login --agent) (default false)
  --cursor
      Opaque cursor from a previous page's `next_cursor`.
  --limit
      Page size.
  --output
      output format: json or table (default json)
  --problem
      Only attempts at this problem ID.
  --server
      server base URL (default $QUIZZOTIC_SERVER or http://localhost:8080)
  --since
      Only attempts answered at or after this RFC 3339 time.
  --tag
      Only attempts at problems carrying this tag, named by ID, slug or alias. An unknown tag is answered 422.
  --until
      Only attempts answered before this RFC 3339 time.

table columns: id, problem_id, score, rating, answered_at

Authentication: QUIZZOTIC_TOKEN, a headless client (QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_ID + QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_SECRET),
or the stored login from "quizzotic login" (--agent for the agent login).

=== quizzotic attempts rate --help ===
usage: quizzotic attempts rate <id> [flags]

Rate an attempt late

Sets the rating of an attempt that has none. The rating can be set
once, and only within 15 minutes of the attempt (`answered_at`); after
that the default rating stands. An `open` attempt submitted without a
rating stays unscheduled and unscored until it is rated here.

The same rules as `POST /attempts` apply: rating 1 (Again) is invalid
for a right `mcq` or `cloze` answer (422 on the `rating` field), and a
wrong one is always Again. A successful rating recomputes the card, and
the response is the same grade, answer and next due date that answering
returns, with the rated attempt.

Returns 409 when the attempt already has a rating (including one sent
with the answer) or when the 15 minutes have passed. Humans only:
agent clients never hold `attempts:write` and get 403.

arguments:
  <id>  Attempt ID.

flags:
  --agent
      authenticate with the stored agent login (see quizzotic login --agent) (default false)
  --data
      request body: @file.json, or - for stdin
  --idempotency-key
      Client-chosen key; replays within 24 h return the original response. [sent as the Idempotency-Key header]
  --output
      output format: json or table (default json)
  --server
      server base URL (default $QUIZZOTIC_SERVER or http://localhost:8080)
  --set
      set a body field: key=value (repeatable; dotted keys nest; values parse as JSON when valid)

Authentication: QUIZZOTIC_TOKEN, a headless client (QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_ID + QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_SECRET),
or the stored login from "quizzotic login" (--agent for the agent login).

=== quizzotic auth --help ===
usage: quizzotic auth <action> [flags]
actions:
  callback         Complete a web login
  login            Start a web login
  logout           End the web session

=== quizzotic auth callback --help ===
usage: quizzotic auth callback [flags]

Complete a web login

The redirect URI registered with the issuer. Requires the
`__Host-quizzotic_login` cookie set by `/auth/login` to match `state`
(a state issued to another browser is rejected with 400 and the cookie
is cleared), then consumes the one-time state, exchanges the code, verifies the ID token (signature, `iss`,
`aud`, `exp`, `nonce`), provisions the user on first login, creates a
server-side session and sets the session cookie (HttpOnly, Secure,
SameSite=Lax, 30-day sliding expiry).

flags:
  --agent
      authenticate with the stored agent login (see quizzotic login --agent) (default false)
  --code
      
  --error
      Error code from the issuer; the login is rejected.
  --output
      output format: json or table (default json)
  --server
      server base URL (default $QUIZZOTIC_SERVER or http://localhost:8080)
  --state
      

Authentication: QUIZZOTIC_TOKEN, a headless client (QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_ID + QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_SECRET),
or the stored login from "quizzotic login" (--agent for the agent login).

=== quizzotic auth login --help ===
usage: quizzotic auth login [flags]

Start a web login

Starts the OIDC Authorization Code + PKCE flow. Generates and stores
state, nonce and the PKCE verifier server-side, then redirects the
browser to the issuer's authorization endpoint. Also sets the
`__Host-quizzotic_login` cookie (HttpOnly, Secure, Path=/, SameSite=Lax,
no Domain, 10-minute lifetime) binding the state to this browser.

flags:
  --agent
      authenticate with the stored agent login (see quizzotic login --agent) (default false)
  --output
      output format: json or table (default json)
  --return_to
      Local path to return to after login. Must start with a single `/`; anything else is ignored and `/` is used.
  --server
      server base URL (default $QUIZZOTIC_SERVER or http://localhost:8080)

Authentication: QUIZZOTIC_TOKEN, a headless client (QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_ID + QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_SECRET),
or the stored login from "quizzotic login" (--agent for the agent login).

=== quizzotic auth logout --help ===
usage: quizzotic auth logout [flags]

End the web session

Deletes the server-side session and clears the cookie. Requires the
session's CSRF token, as form field `csrf_token` or header
`X-CSRF-Token`. With no valid session it only clears the cookie.

flags:
  --agent
      authenticate with the stored agent login (see quizzotic login --agent) (default false)
  --output
      output format: json or table (default json)
  --server
      server base URL (default $QUIZZOTIC_SERVER or http://localhost:8080)

Authentication: QUIZZOTIC_TOKEN, a headless client (QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_ID + QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_SECRET),
or the stored login from "quizzotic login" (--agent for the agent login).

