or the stored login from "quizzotic login" (--agent for the agent login).

=== quizzotic problems create-batch --help ===
usage: quizzotic problems create-batch [flags]

Create up to 100 problems at once

Creates every item (a problem plus its tags) in one transaction. The
batch holds 1 to 100 items. If any item is invalid, nothing is written
and the 422 response lists the invalid fields of every bad item in
`errors`, each `field` prefixed with the item's index, for example
`items[3].payload.choices` or `items[0].tags[1]`. Items are validated
like `problems.create`; each tag is an ID, slug or alias of one of the
caller's tags (a merged tag resolves to the tag it was merged into).
The created problems are returned in request order. The request body
is limited to 1 MiB.

flags:
  --agent
      authenticate with the stored agent login (see quizzotic login --agent) (default false)
  --data
      request body: @file.json, or - for stdin
  --idempotency-key
      Client-chosen key; replays within 24 h return the original response. [sent as the Idempotency-Key header]
  --output
      output format: json or table (default json)
  --server
      server base URL (default $QUIZZOTIC_SERVER or http://localhost:8080)
  --set
      set a body field: key=value (repeatable; dotted keys nest; values parse as JSON when valid)

Authentication: QUIZZOTIC_TOKEN, a headless client (QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_ID + QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_SECRET),
or the stored login from "quizzotic login" (--agent for the agent login).

=== quizzotic problems delete --help ===
usage: quizzotic problems delete <id> [flags]

Delete a problem

Soft-deletes the problem from any status. Versions and attempts are
kept; the problem stops appearing in reads and lists. Requires
`If-Match` (412 when stale, 428 when missing). Deleting an already
deleted problem is 404.

arguments:
  <id>  A problem ID.

flags:
  --agent
      authenticate with the stored agent login (see quizzotic login --agent) (default false)
  --if-match
      ETag of the resource version being updated. A stale value returns 412. [sent as the If-Match header]
  --output
      output format: json or table (default json)
  --server
      server base URL (default $QUIZZOTIC_SERVER or http://localhost:8080)

Authentication: QUIZZOTIC_TOKEN, a headless client (QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_ID + QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_SECRET),
or the stored login from "quizzotic login" (--agent for the agent login).

=== quizzotic problems edit --help ===
usage: quizzotic problems edit <id> [flags]

Edit a problem

Creates a new version from the current one with the given fields
replaced; omitted fields keep their value. `change_kind` is required:
`minor` (typo, wording) keeps the card; `major` (different correct
answer or question) starts a new card epoch, so earlier attempts stay
attached to the old epoch. The merged result is validated like a
create. Requires `If-Match` (412 when stale, 428 when missing).

arguments:
  <id>  

flags:
  --agent
      authenticate with the stored agent login (see quizzotic login --agent) (default false)
  --data
      request body: @file.json, or - for stdin
  --if-match
      ETag of the resource version being updated. A stale value returns 412. [sent as the If-Match header]
  --output
      output format: json or table (default json)
  --server
      server base URL (default $QUIZZOTIC_SERVER or http://localhost:8080)
  --set
      set a body field: key=value (repeatable; dotted keys nest; values parse as JSON when valid)

Authentication: QUIZZOTIC_TOKEN, a headless client (QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_ID + QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_SECRET),
or the stored login from "quizzotic login" (--agent for the agent login).

=== quizzotic problems get --help ===
usage: quizzotic problems get <id> [flags]

Get a problem

Returns the problem's current version. The default `full` view
includes correct answers, reference answer and rubric. `view=prompt`
is what a client shows while answering: no correct answers, reference
answer, rubric or explanation, and MCQ choices shuffled when the
payload says `shuffle`.

arguments:
  <id>  

flags:
  --agent
      authenticate with the stored agent login (see quizzotic login --agent) (default false)
  --output
      output format: json or table (default json)
  --server
      server base URL (default $QUIZZOTIC_SERVER or http://localhost:8080)
  --view
      Which view to return. Defaults to `full`. (one of: full, prompt)

Authentication: QUIZZOTIC_TOKEN, a headless client (QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_ID + QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_SECRET),
or the stored login from "quizzotic login" (--agent for the agent login).

=== quizzotic problems list --help ===
usage: quizzotic problems list [flags]

List problems

Lists the caller's non-deleted problems, oldest first, with cursor
pagination. Filters combine with AND. `type` and `q` apply to the
problem's current version, `created_by_kind` to its creator. `q` is a
case-insensitive substring match over the prompt. `tag` accepts a tag
slug or ID.

flags:
  --agent
      authenticate with the stored agent login (see quizzotic login --agent) (default false)
  --created_by_kind
      Only problems created by this kind of actor. (one of: human, agent, system)
  --cursor
      Opaque cursor from a previous page's `next_cursor`.
  --limit
      Page size.
  --output
      output format: json or table (default json)
  --q
      Case-insensitive substring of the prompt.
  --server
      server base URL (default $QUIZZOTIC_SERVER or http://localhost:8080)
  --status
      Only problems in this status. (one of: draft, live, archived)
  --tag
      Only problems carrying this tag, named by ID, slug or alias (a merged tag stands for the tag it was merged into). An unknown tag is answered 422.
  --type
      Only problems of this type. (one of: mcq, cloze, open)

table columns: id, status, type, version, prompt

Authentication: QUIZZOTIC_TOKEN, a headless client (QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_ID + QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_SECRET),
or the stored login from "quizzotic login" (--agent for the agent login).

