or the stored login from "quizzotic login" (--agent for the agent login).

=== quizzotic sessions create --help ===
usage: quizzotic sessions create [flags]

Start a review or quiz session

Builds and freezes the ordered list of problems to work through, and
returns it. Humans only: `sessions:write` is never granted to agents.

`kind: review` collects the caller's due cards (lowest current recall
first, within the daily review budget) and a weighted sample of new
problems (within the daily new-card budget), interleaving one new card
after every `new_interval` reviews. The same session ID over the same
data always builds the same list. The daily budgets are measured
against the attempt log of the caller's study day, so quiz answers
count toward them like any other answer.

`kind: quiz` serves the live problems of the quiz named by `quiz_id`
in authored order, or shuffled when `shuffle` is true. The quiz must be
`live`; a draft or archived quiz is refused with 422, and so is
`shuffle` on a review session. Daily limits do not apply to a quiz.
Answers update cards like any other attempt.

A session with nothing to serve is valid: it is created with no items,
and `next` reports that nothing remains. Answers join the session by
sending its `id` as `session_id` to `POST /attempts`.

flags:
  --agent
      authenticate with the stored agent login (see quizzotic login --agent) (default false)
  --data
      request body: @file.json, or - for stdin
  --idempotency-key
      Client-chosen key; replays within 24 h return the original response. [sent as the Idempotency-Key header]
  --output
      output format: json or table (default json)
  --server
      server base URL (default $QUIZZOTIC_SERVER or http://localhost:8080)
  --set
      set a body field: key=value (repeatable; dotted keys nest; values parse as JSON when valid)

Authentication: QUIZZOTIC_TOKEN, a headless client (QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_ID + QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_SECRET),
or the stored login from "quizzotic login" (--agent for the agent login).

=== quizzotic sessions get --help ===
usage: quizzotic sessions get <id> [flags]

Get a session

Returns the session with its frozen list, marking which items have been
answered. An item is answered when the caller has sent an attempt with
this session's ID for its problem. Humans only.

arguments:
  <id>  Session ID.

flags:
  --agent
      authenticate with the stored agent login (see quizzotic login --agent) (default false)
  --output
      output format: json or table (default json)
  --server
      server base URL (default $QUIZZOTIC_SERVER or http://localhost:8080)

Authentication: QUIZZOTIC_TOKEN, a headless client (QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_ID + QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_SECRET),
or the stored login from "quizzotic login" (--agent for the agent login).

=== quizzotic sessions next --help ===
usage: quizzotic sessions next <id> [flags]

Get the next problem of a session

Returns the first unanswered item of the session as a prompt (no
correct answers, reference answer or explanation), and how many
unanswered items remain, this one included. Items whose problem is no
longer live are skipped.

For a review session, learning-step cards that have come due since the
session started are first appended to its list, so a card answered
Again is offered again once its step has elapsed. `item` is null when
nothing is left to serve right now; a learning card that is not yet due
may still be appended by a later call. Returns 409 once the session is
completed. Humans only.

arguments:
  <id>  Session ID.

flags:
  --agent
      authenticate with the stored agent login (see quizzotic login --agent) (default false)
  --output
      output format: json or table (default json)
  --server
      server base URL (default $QUIZZOTIC_SERVER or http://localhost:8080)

Authentication: QUIZZOTIC_TOKEN, a headless client (QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_ID + QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_SECRET),
or the stored login from "quizzotic login" (--agent for the agent login).

=== quizzotic tag-operations --help ===
usage: quizzotic tag-operations <action> [flags]
actions:
  apply            Apply a proposed tag operation
  get              Get a tag operation
  list             List tag operations
  propose          Propose a tag operation
  reject           Reject a proposed tag operation
  revert           Revert an applied tag operation

=== quizzotic tag-operations apply --help ===
usage: quizzotic tag-operations apply <id> [flags]

Apply a proposed tag operation

Applies a proposed operation in one transaction: captures the
before-snapshot, rewrites the tag rows, aliases and problem mappings,
and records the decider. The payload is validated again against the
current state (422 or 409 when it no longer holds). An operation that
is already decided is a 409.

arguments:
  <id>  Tag operation ID.

flags:
  --agent
      authenticate with the stored agent login (see quizzotic login --agent) (default false)
  --idempotency-key
      Client-chosen key; replays within 24 h return the original response. [sent as the Idempotency-Key header]
  --output
      output format: json or table (default json)
  --server
      server base URL (default $QUIZZOTIC_SERVER or http://localhost:8080)

Authentication: QUIZZOTIC_TOKEN, a headless client (QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_ID + QUIZZOTIC_CLIENT_SECRET),
or the stored login from "quizzotic login" (--agent for the agent login).

